<%= render layout: 'blogs/blog_post_layout', locals: { article: article } do %>
  <p class="lead">You gave your AI access to all your docs. It still makes things up. Here's why naive RAG fails and how to fix it.</p>

  <h2>Why Naive RAG Fails</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bad chunking</strong>—splitting on character count breaks context and splits key information across chunks.</li>
    <li><strong>Wrong embedding model</strong>—trained on the wrong domain; retrieval quality suffers.</li>
    <li><strong>Low retrieval precision</strong>—wrong docs in the top-k.</li>
    <li><strong>No re-ranking</strong>—the best chunk isn't first; the LLM focuses on the wrong one.</li>
    <li><strong>Poor prompt engineering</strong>—the model ignores or underweights the retrieved context.</li>
    <li><strong>No "I don't know"</strong>—when retrieval score is low, the model answers anyway and hallucinates.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Anatomy of Good RAG</h2>
  <p><strong>Chunking:</strong> Semantic chunking with overlap so meaning isn't split. <strong>Embeddings:</strong> Domain-specific or fine-tuned for your content. <strong>Vector DB:</strong> pgvector, Pinecone, or Qdrant with proper indexing. <strong>Hybrid search:</strong> Semantic + BM25 keyword so you don't miss exact terms. <strong>Re-ranking:</strong> Cross-encoder over top-k to put the best chunk on top. <strong>Prompt:</strong> Clear template that says "answer only from context; if not found say so." <strong>Confidence:</strong> If retrieval score is below threshold, don't answer—escalate or say "I don't know."</p>

  <h2>Real Example: Legal RAG 60% → 92%</h2>
  <p>Fixing chunking, switching to a legal-tuned embedding, adding hybrid search and re-ranking, and a strict "don't guess" prompt took accuracy from 60% to 92%. We'll cover code for semantic chunking, hybrid search, and confidence-based answering in the full article.</p>

  <p>When RAG isn't enough: for highly specialized, consistent tasks, fine-tuning may beat RAG. Evaluation metrics: precision, recall, F1 on a held-out set. <a href="https://calendly.com/ahmadkamran/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Schedule a RAG system audit</a>.</p>
<% end %>
